  {
    "episode_id": 88483,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/8/88483.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 8,
    "turn_text": "Well, you know, like most big societies, it's complicated, right? There were some things that China did quite well, some things that they did that were not right at all. We still don't know the origin of this virus, and it's important for us to figure that out. It's also, you know, yes, they covered up. They made some serious mistakes. They were dishonest about this in some respects. On the other hand, very early on, Chinese scientists put the entire genome sequence of the virus online, and that enabled American scientists to begin working on a vaccine and treatment immediately long before we had any samples of this virus. So now, yes, there's someone in the propaganda machine over in China blaming the United States of America. That's absolutely preposterous, obviously. But that's the kind of thing that authoritarian governments do sometimes. I think we should be very clear-eyed about this. Yeah, the Chinese actually handled this better than the last virus outbreak that came from China, but not nearly the way they should have.",
